## First-run welcome
marmara-welcome-language-title = Welcome to Marmara
marmara-welcome-language-sub = Choose your language. The change applies after a restart.
marmara-welcome-terms-title = Marmara Browser Terms of Use
marmara-welcome-terms-sub = Version 1 · Last updated: 30 October 2026
marmara-welcome-terms-1-h = 1. General
marmara-welcome-terms-1-p = Marmara Browser (“Marmara”) is a privacy-first web browser. By ticking "I have read and accept the terms" you are deemed to have accepted the articles below.
marmara-welcome-terms-2-h = 2. No data collection
marmara-welcome-terms-2-p = As Marmara's developers, we do not collect any data from you through the application on our own behalf. Your history, bookmarks, passwords and settings are stored only on this computer. Data sent to the third-party services below is not collected by us; it is the responsibility of those services.
marmara-welcome-terms-3-h = 3. LibreWolf and Firefox
marmara-welcome-terms-3-p = Marmara is not officially affiliated with LibreWolf; it is a fork of LibreWolf and is therefore built on Firefox. LibreWolf tries to block the telemetry that Firefox collects, but it does not guarantee that it does. The licenses of these components apply. Marmara is not developed or endorsed by the Mozilla Foundation, the LibreWolf project or the GNOME Project. Firefox is a trademark of the Mozilla Foundation; GNOME is a trademark of the GNOME Foundation.
marmara-welcome-terms-4-h = 4. Third-party components and services
marmara-welcome-terms-4-p1 = Marmara uses the following third-party components that come preinstalled: uBlock Origin, Privacy Badger, ClearURLs and the ToS;DR service. They are not affiliated with Marmara; they are provided by their own developers and are subject to their own terms and privacy policies. Marmara is not responsible for how these components work or for the data they collect. You can turn them off or remove them at any time.
marmara-welcome-terms-4-p2 = Marmara also communicates with the following services when you use or enable them:
marmara-welcome-terms-4-li1 = The search engine you choose (when you search; search suggestions are off by default)
marmara-welcome-terms-4-li2 = The add-on store, addons.mozilla.org (when installing and updating extensions)
marmara-welcome-terms-4-li3 = ToS;DR (only if you turn it on; the domain name of the site you visit; ToS;DR data is provided under a CC BY-SA license)
marmara-welcome-terms-4-li4 = An encrypted DNS provider (only if you turn it on)
marmara-welcome-terms-5-h = 5. GitHub
marmara-welcome-terms-5-p = During update checks, Marmara may connect to GitHub to find out the latest version. GitHub's own terms and privacy policy apply to that connection.
marmara-welcome-terms-6-h = 6. License and trademark
marmara-welcome-terms-6-p = Marmara is provided under the Mozilla Public License 2.0; its source code is at https://github.com/fuzuliorg/marmara. The names Marmara Browser and Marmara Tarayıcı and the Marmara logo belong to Fuzuli Initiative and are also subject to the rules in the TRADEMARK.md file in the Marmara repository. The names and logos of LibreWolf, Firefox, GNOME and the search engines belong to their respective owners. Marmara's interface icons are based on the GNOME Adwaita icon theme (LGPL-3.0 or CC BY-SA 3.0) and the start page uses the Inter typeface (SIL Open Font License 1.1); the license texts are in the licenses folder of the application package.
marmara-welcome-terms-7-h = 7. Disclaimer of warranty and limitation of liability
marmara-welcome-terms-7-p = Marmara is provided as is. No warranty of any kind, express or implied, is given, including fitness for a particular purpose, uninterrupted operation or freedom from errors. To the extent permitted by law, the developers cannot be held liable for direct or indirect damages arising from the use of Marmara. The sites you visit, the files you download and the extensions you install are your responsibility.
marmara-welcome-terms-8-h = 8. Changes
marmara-welcome-terms-8-p = We may update these terms. Important changes appear in a new release and in this text's version number; continuing to use the application after an update means you accept the new terms.
marmara-welcome-terms-9-h = 9. Governing law
marmara-welcome-terms-9-p = These terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of Türkiye.
marmara-welcome-terms-10-h = 10. Contact and data shared by email
marmara-welcome-terms-10-p = For questions, you can write to marmara.browser@proton.me or reach out through the GitHub issues page. If you email us, your email address, your name (if given) and the content of your message are processed by Fuzuli Initiative as the data controller. This information is used only to answer your request and resolve the matter; it is not used for marketing and is not shared with third parties except where required by law. Emails are kept on the servers of our email provider, Proton Mail (Switzerland). Once the matter is closed, the correspondence is deleted within 3 months at the latest; if a legal obligation or a dispute requires it, it is kept for as long as that requires. Under Turkey's Personal Data Protection Law No. 6698 you have the right to access your data and to ask for it to be corrected or deleted; you can write to the same address, and we will conclude your request within 30 days at the latest. What you write on GitHub is subject to GitHub's terms.
marmara-welcome-terms-accept = I have read and accept the terms
marmara-welcome-theme-title = Choose the look
marmara-welcome-theme-sub = Follow the system, or pick the light or dark theme.
marmara-welcome-search-title = Choose your search engine
marmara-welcome-search-sub = Used in the address bar and on new tabs. You can change it any time in Settings.
marmara-welcome-tosdr-title = Terms of Service ratings
marmara-welcome-tosdr-sub = Marmara can show a ToS;DR grade for the site you visit in the address bar. To do that it sends the site's domain name (such as example.com) to ToS;DR. Nothing is sent from private windows. You can change this any time in Settings.
marmara-welcome-tosdr-off = Don't show ratings
marmara-welcome-tosdr-on = Show ratings (domain names are sent to ToS;DR)
marmara-welcome-passwords-title = Saving passwords
marmara-welcome-passwords-sub = Marmara can offer to save your passwords when you sign in. They are stored only on this computer. You can change this any time in Settings.
